      "en": "Nonstop flights from the UK to Saudi Arabia exist only from Heathrow and Manchester, both to Jeddah: Heathrow on Saudia and British Airways at about 6h05, Manchester on Saudia at about 6h27. Birmingham has no nonstop, and no UK airport sells a nonstop to Madinah. In the 14 November 2026 KAYAK snapshot the cheapest Heathrow return was £347 with stops and £669 nonstop, Manchester £326 and £515, Birmingham £354 with two stops. Two rules outrank price: the FCDO advisory, and the Hajj-season restriction that can stop a non-Hajj visitor boarding a flight to Jeddah, Madinah or Taif.",
